Little White Mouse makes a very interesting point that the blue jelly
room is a form of death and not really living.  I want to play a game
and not just switch rings for all of enternity.  I want to live a life
and not a form of death.  So, what is the definition of live?  You
work, you play, you make food, you take care of pets and you save for
the next generation.

The blue jelly solution is the result of a prior discussion and as such
has been rejected as a solution in the re-asking of this question.  The
point of this discussion is to create a new more fun solution.  A
solution that you would want in real life or at least want to play and
not sit in a corner, afraid, for all enternity.

Playing Nethack for the sake of playing Nethack is more fun than
playing computer solitaire.



